Description: Wild OS style gallery cards
 The style gallery (.uno:StylesPreview) shows each style as a card, as in
 the Wild OS design boards and Word's gallery: "Aa" in the style's font,
 colour, weight and slant over the style's name, on paper white, the
 current style's card outlined in the accent colour. The view keeps no
 selection of its own, so the outline always follows the style at the
 cursor. Writer's gallery shows Body Text, Title, Heading 1, Heading 2 and
 Quotations, the document's own styles staying in the Styles deck.
 LibreOffice Online keeps the previews it had.
Author: Wild OS Developers <dev@wildos.io>
Forwarded: not-needed

